   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Analyse factorielle"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "65676c2b",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "The goal of this section is to explore the relation of the explainatory variables with the target variable. Here we will use PCA, LDA for the quantitative variables, then MCA for the qualitaitive."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "4ce5d1a1",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### PCA"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 32,
   "id": "60686b2c",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from sklearn.preprocessing import StandardScaler\n",
    "from sklearn.decomposition import PCA"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 33,
   "id": "4295a7b8",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "data_pca = numeric_df\n",
    "scaler = StandardScaler()\n",
    "data_scaled = scaler.fit_transform(data_pca)\n",
    "pca = PCA()\n",
    "respca = pca.fit_transform(data_scaled)\n",
    "explained_variance = pca.explained_variance_ratio_"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 34,
   "id": "cf7aa50a",
   "metadata": {},
